> Read the origin and non-power-of-two head order

Sinusoidal position0 alternates0,1. Three ALiBi heads use slopes1/16,1/256,1/4 in the authors ordering. A naive geometric progression over three heads gives a different result.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/transformer_positions_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;std::filesystem::create_directories("build");auto slopes=m::AlibiSlopes(3);auto values=n::concat({n::select(m::SinusoidalTable(2,4),0,0),n::from_vector(slopes)},0);if(slopes!=std::vector<float>{1.f/16,1.f/256,1.f/4})return 1;
std::print("| coordinate | computed value |\n|---:|---:|\n");auto v=values.to_vector<double>();for(size_t i=0;i<v.size();++i)std::print("| {} | {:.9f} |\n",i,v[i]);n::save_npz("build/transformer_positions_worked.npz",{{"values",values}});dm::graphics::RPlot::create().bars(n::arange(0,std::int64_t(v.size())).to_vector<double>(),v,"native values",{37,99,235}).title("Read the origin and non-power-of-two head order").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/transformer_positions_worked.svg");}
